  <div class="author-profile-body">
    <p>Guille Ojeda is the author of all articles on <a href="/">AWS for Engineers</a>. He writes about AWS and cloud architecture for software engineers, with a focus on understanding how cloud services work and when to use them.</p>
    <p>He is a Principal Innovation Architect at Caylent and an author and speaker on AWS and applied AI. His work includes the <a href="https://newsletter.simpleaws.dev/">Simple AWS newsletter</a> and the books <cite>Node.js on AWS</cite> and <cite>AWS Made Simple and Fun</cite>.</p>
    <p>The guides on AWS for Engineers are developed with AI assistance. Guille is responsible for their authorship and published content.</p>
    <p>Find his current work, books, talks, and professional background on <a href="https://guilleojeda.com/" rel="me">his personal website</a> and <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/guilleojeda/" rel="me">LinkedIn</a>.</p>
